node_modules
.env
dist/
.astro/
*.key
# Match by PATTERN, not by exact filename. Rotating a key naturally produces
# neighbours -- google_service_account.json.dead, .bak, .old, or the
# <project>-<keyid>.json that Cloud Console hands you -- and an exact-name rule
# ignores the file you named while leaving every one of its siblings visible to
# `git add -A`. This repo is public; a private key needs to be unstageable by
# accident, not merely by the one spelling somebody thought of.
google_service_account.json*
*service_account*.json
*service-account*.json
# Cloud Console names a downloaded key <project-id>-<12 hex>.json, which matches
# none of the patterns above. Anchored to twelve hex characters so it cannot catch
# package.json, tsconfig.json, pulseData.json or anything else legitimate.
*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f].json
*.pem
scratch/
# Tooling lives in devops/ and CI-run tools there are TRACKED. Only these two
# subfolders are ignored: devops/local/ is one-off scratch (the retired pulse
# seeders moved there from scripts/), devops/reports/ is generated output.
# Never ignore devops/ wholesale -- CI invokes those tools from the checkout.
devops/local/
devops/reports/
test_articles.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc


